UID:1YKiphvwfXnSHYEZKbsQO
SUMMARY:Sound Bath with Daemein Smith (Prioritizing Peace)
DTSTAMP:20260814T042948Z
DTSTART:20260926T080000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a peaceful morning experience in Hermann Park with 
	a free guided Sound Bath led by Daemein Smith of Prioritizing Peace. Set a
	gainst the natural beauty of the Tsuru Family Terrace in the Commons\, thi
	s immersive meditation experience uses sound and vibration to promote rela
	xation\, mindfulness\, and emotional well-being. Guests are encouraged to 
	slow down\, reset\, and “Prioritize Peace” through a calming journey of so
	und healing in nature. \n Tsuru Family Terrace\n Saturday\, September 26\n
	 8 – 9 a.m.\n Free Community Session \nGuests are encouraged to bring a yo
	ga mat if available. Blankets and pillows are also recommended for additio
	nal comfort. All ages and experience levels welcome. \nParking: Free parki
	ng available across the street from the Commons in Lot S (6215 Main St\, H
	ouston\, TX 77030). Additional street parking available along Main Street.
	\n\nhttps://hermannpark.org/event/sound-bath-with-daemein-smith-prioritizi
	ng-peace-14/\n\nFrom Hermann Park Conservancy
URL:https://hermannpark.org/event/sound-bath-with-daemein-smith-prioritizin
	g-peace-14/
LOCATION:The Commons
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:hermann-park
CATEGORIES:Hermann Park Conservancy
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT1H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://architecturehousto
 n.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/History-of-Street-Skating-1.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://architecturehouston.org/wp-content/upload
 s/2026/05/History-of-Street-Skating-1.jpg
UID:hUl3oZaOlgF4Jr559rMz-
SUMMARY:The Architectural History of Houston Street Skating
DTSTAMP:20260814T042948Z
DTSTART:20260926T090000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join lifelong skateboarder and architectural historian Ted Barr
	ow on a walking tour of the highlights of Houston’s Modernist and Late-Mod
	ernist architecture through a skateboarder’s perspective. The tour will co
	ver key plazas and buildings which became local\, state-wide\, and eventua
	lly global skateboarding destinations from the late 1980’s to today. \n\nA
	bout Ted Barrow \nTheodore (Ted) Barrow is an art historian\, writer\, cur
	ator\, and lecturer whose work bridges academic scholarship and contempora
	ry currents. Born in Bolinas\, California\, he holds a Ph.D. in art histor
	y from the Graduate Center\, CUNY\, where he explored the Florida painting
	s of Winslow Homer and John Singer Sargent through an ecocritical lens. Ba
	rrow has taught at Barnard College\, Baruch College\, City College of New 
	York\, and the University of San Francisco. Outside of art and academia\, 
	he is a distinctive voice in skateboarding culture\, known for This Old Le
	dge\, a video series that investigates the cultural and architectural sign
	ificance of global skate spots.” \n  \nThis program is in conjunction with
	 The Kinetics of Urban Movement\, on view at the Architecture Center Houst
	on from June 18-September 26. \n  \nExhibition Sponsors and Community Part
	ners \nKinetics of Urban Movement is funded in part by the City of Houston
	 through Houston Arts Alliance \n \nCherries Wheels\nHoney Skate Club\nHou
	ston Parks and Recreation Department\nHouston Skate Academy\nSelect\nSkate
	 ECOSYSTEMS\nSouthside Skatepark\n\nhttps://architecturehouston.org/event/
	the-architectural-history-of-houston-street-skating/\n\nFrom AIA Houston
URL:https://architecturehouston.org/event/the-architectural-history-of-hous
	ton-street-skating/
LOCATION:Tranquility Park\, 400 Rusk\, Houston\, Texas\, 77002
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:aia-houston
CATEGORIES:AIA Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://hermannpark.org/wp
 -content/uploads/2024/04/mcg_mount4-e1757000165605.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://hermannpark.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/0
 4/mcg_mount4-e1757000165605.jpg
UID:RmtVpr5HKs9VZ9kWSsAc0
SUMMARY:National Public Lands Day
DTSTAMP:20260814T042948Z
DTSTART:20260926T090000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Saturday\, September 26\, for National Public Lands 
	Day\, the nation’s largest single-day volunteer event for public lands! Th
	is is your chance to give back to Hermann Park\, one of Houston’s most che
	rished green spaces. \nWhether you’re pulling invasive weeds\, planting na
	tive grasses or helping with trail maintenance\, your time and energy will
	 directly support the health and beauty of the park for generations to com
	e. \nAll ages welcome – no experience necessary! Bring your friends\, fami
	ly\, or coworkers and help us make a lasting impact. \nSign up for a sessi
	on at McGovern Centennial Gardens\, the Commons\, or the Heart of the Park
	 HERE.\n\nhttps://hermannpark.org/event/national-public-lands-day/\n\nFrom
	 Hermann Park Conservancy
URL:https://hermannpark.org/event/national-public-lands-day/
LOCATION:McGovern Centennial Gardens\, 1500 Hermann Drive\, Houston\, TX\, 
	77004\, United States
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:hermann-park
CATEGORIES:Hermann Park Conservancy
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT3H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://houstonarboretum.or
 g/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Phenology-1280-x-720.png
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://houstonarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/05/Phenology-1280-x-720.png
UID:2XE_njutAS7LROMdK6NEM
SUMMARY:Fourth Saturday Phenology Walk
DTSTAMP:20260814T042948Z
DTSTART:20260926T090000Z
DESCRIPTION:Fourth Saturday of the Month9:00 – 11:00 amFree\, donations app
	reciatedAll ages\, minors must be accompanied by an adult \n\n\n\nMeet in 
	front of the Nature Center building \n\n\n\nDiscover the hidden seasonal r
	hythms of nature firsthand on our guided Phenology Walks\, where we track 
	the life cycles of different plants across ecosystems\, from the first spr
	ing bud burst to winter dormancy. You’ll learn how shifting weather patter
	ns and climate change influence the timing of these important events in ou
	r local ecosystems and how you can become a community scientist\, contribu
	ting vital data from your own backyard to a global research initiative.  \
	n\n\n\nThese relaxing morning walks are led by scientists from Rice Univer
	sity and staff from the Arboretum. We welcome nature enthusiasts of all ag
	es\, however kids 12 years and younger must be accompanied by a guardian. 
	\n\n\n\nLearn more about the study of phenology and ways you can contribut
	e at https://www.usanpn.org/nn \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCommunity Science Partner\n
	\nhttps://houstonarboretum.org/event/fourth-saturday-phenology-walk/2026-0
	9-26/\n\nFrom Houston Arboretum & Nature Center
URL:https://houstonarboretum.org/event/fourth-saturday-phenology-walk/2026-
	09-26/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:houston-arboretum
CATEGORIES:Houston Arboretum & Nature Center
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
